{:id "0031-lab-debug"
 :title "Lab ?debug overlay: frame rate, frame time, frame number and the cues as they fire"
 :lupa/deps #{"0030-lab-stage"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :low
 :goal "Ben is recording screen videos of the lab on his M5 (WebGPU) for
        the foreman, who reads them as still frames. With /lab/?debug, every
        video frame should carry its own numbers: which frame it is, the
        time, the frame rate and frame times, the backend, how many glyphs
        are drawn, and which cues just fired (word, effect, intensity,
        source), so what Ben felt can be tied to what the code did."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/debug.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/debug_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "public/lab/index.html" "e2e/lab.mjs"
         "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "halfahead.lab.debug (.cljc, pure):
            (record stats now-ms) -> stats with this frame added: keep the
              timestamps of the last 1000 ms of frames and a running frame
              count.
            (summary stats) -> {:frame n :fps f :mean-ms m :worst-ms w}
              over the window (fps from the frames in the last second; mean
              and worst of the gaps between consecutive frames; zeros when
              there are fewer than two frames).
            (new-cues old-draft new-draft) -> the placed cues in new-draft
              that are not in old-draft, as
              [{:word :effect :intensity :source :at-ms} ...] in order.
            (cue-log log cues now-ms) -> the last 6 entries, newest first,
              dropping entries older than 8000 ms.
          main.cljs: when the page URL has a debug query parameter
          (?debug or ?debug=1), keep stats and the cue log in the atom (via
          the pure fns above) and, every frame, write a small overlay:
            frame 1234 · t 12.345 s · 60 fps · mean 16.6 ms · worst 18.0 ms
            WebGPU · 36 glyphs
            then one line per recent cue: deploy -> launch 0.9 (glossary)
          Without ?debug nothing changes and no stats are kept.
          index.html: the overlay element, bottom-left, monospace, small,
          high contrast on the dark stage, aria-hidden, pointer-events none,
          hidden unless debug is on. It must not cover the text block.
          e2e/lab.mjs: a step that opens /lab/?debug, types \"we shipped it \",
          and asserts the overlay shows a frame number greater than 10, an
          fps value, the backend, and a line containing \"shipped -> launch\";
          then that /lab/ without debug has no visible overlay."
 :acceptance
 ["debug tests: summary over a synthetic 60 Hz sequence gives fps 60 (+-1)
   and mean ~16.7 ms; a single 50 ms gap shows as worst 50; fewer than two
   frames gives zeros; new-cues returns exactly the cues added by an edit;
   cue-log keeps at most 6, newest first, and drops entries over 8 s old"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the new debug step; `bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["No change to motion, cues, the renderer's drawing, or the schema"
  "No logging to the network or storage; the overlay is display only"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/draft.cljc"
           "public/lab/index.html" "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"
           "src/halfahead/schema.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
